{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1540401049,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQzMjc0NjIyNQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2945#issuecomment-432746225"},"message":"First of all: Thanks for pointing out your view on this. We are actually working on that. At least in parts you can already have what you want.\nYou might want to have a look at `datalad-run-procedure` (plus I'd recommend datalad-container extension: https://github.com/datalad/datalad-container)\nOur current approach on that:\nHave a dataset with registered procedures (and possibly containers to be used) for those analyses. Such a dataset can come with appropriate metadata of course and can be discovered that way. By installing it as a subdataset into the dataset that contains the to-be analysed data, you make those procedures (and containers) available.\nA procedure in a subdataset can be referenced from the superdataset via `mysubds/myprocedure` where `myprocedure` would be the name of the very same procedure if referred to from the subdataset itself (same for containers).\n`run-procedure``should work with `rerun` as well. That's what I'm currently working on and hopefully it gets somewhat streamlined and better documented soon.\nIn addition @mih is working on remote execution that could be rerun as well (even locally). It might be worth having a look at https://github.com/datalad/datalad-htcondor wrt this aspect.","files":null},{"type":6,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1540401049,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDE0NDA3MTA2Mw=="},"target":"ffe2deccc881d4b2407bf18ed67a47f8e9015406f5a24aca328a798478ba95b1","message":"First of all: Thanks for pointing out your view on this. We are actually working on that. At least in parts you can already have what you want.\nYou might want to have a look at `datalad-run-procedure` (plus I'd recommend datalad-container extension: https://github.com/datalad/datalad-container)\nOur current approach on that:\nHave a dataset with registered procedures (and possibly containers to be used) for those analyses. Such a dataset can come with appropriate metadata of course and can be discovered that way. By installing it as a subdataset into the dataset that contains the to-be analysed data, you make those procedures (and containers) available.\nA procedure in a subdataset can be referenced from the superdataset via `mysubds/myprocedure` where `myprocedure` would be the name of the very same procedure if referred to from the subdataset itself (same for containers).\n`run-procedure` should work with `rerun` as well. That's what I'm currently working on and hopefully it gets somewhat streamlined and better documented soon.\nIn addition @mih is working on remote execution that could be rerun as well (even locally). It might be worth having a look at https://github.com/datalad/datalad-htcondor wrt this aspect.","files":null}]}